  "dom_id": "step-q127809",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Determine the interval on which the function $f(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,2{e}^{t-1},\\,\\sqrt{5-t}⟩$ is continuous.",
  "worked_solution": "A vector-valued function is continuous on an interval if and only if each of its components is continuous on that interval.\n\nLet's now consider the components of $f(t)$ one by one.\n\n- The function $t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t$ is continuous for all real numbers.\n\n- The function $2{e}^{t-1}$ is continuous for all real numbers.\n\n- The function $\\sqrt{5-t}$ is continuous for $t\\le 5.$\n\nTherefore, the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is continuous for $t\\le 5.$ So the interval of continuity is $(-\\infty ,5].$",
